{"parentUuid":"d5fcb337-ba4c-456b-bc32-8462496ecaec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019uPR11dSYanjHF1VVzpd4M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" The H drive has filesystem corruption in the `.claude` directory — PowerShell returned a partial listing before hitting an unreadable error. I can see some directories like agents, bin, cache, commands, and docs are still accessible, but the drive's integrity is compromised.\n\nThe real issue is that the hooks directory and everything after it are likely inaccessible due to the corruption, which explains why SessionStart is failing — Node can't read those .mjs files. The data probably isn't deleted, just unreachable because the filesystem index is damaged. I need to stop writing to the H drive immediately to prevent further corruption, then either run chkdsk to attempt repair or carefully extract what's still readable to a safe location first before deciding on recovery steps.","signature":"":null},{"error":"{\"parentUuid\":\"49a0f5bf-28fe-47fd-86e6-4d5fbfe1bd28\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"attachment\":{\"type\":\"hook_success\",\"hookName\":\"PostToolUse:Bash\",\"toolUseID\":\"toolu_01CzJetwjWD5abxqq2dh88Cu\",\"hookEvent\":\"Pos","fix":null},{"error":"{\"parentUuid\":\"4e215f5e-51d8-48cd-bd84-108bda890de3\",\"isSidechain\":false,\"attachment\":{\"type\":\"hook_success\",\"hookName\":\"PostToolUse:Bash\",\"toolUseID\":\"toolu_01CzJetwjWD5abxqq2dh88Cu\",\"hookEvent\":\"Pos","fix":null}],"tokens_spent":null,"tokens_by_category":null,"success_signals":44,"failure_signals":16}
